@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
}

<div class="page-head">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>What is stored, and why</p>
</div>

<div class="prose">
    <p>
        Weather Seeker stores as little as it can. There is no advertising, no analytics service,
        and no third-party tracker on any page.
    </p>

    <h2>Account data</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Username</strong> — stored so you can sign in, and shown in the header while you are signed in.</li>
        <li><strong>Password</strong> — stored only as a one-way hash. The original text is never written to disk or logged.</li>
        <li><strong>Account ID</strong> — assigned by the database when the account is created.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Session</h2>
    <p>
        Signing in sets a single authentication cookie. It is <code>HttpOnly</code>, <code>Secure</code>,
        <code>SameSite=Lax</code>, and expires after eight hours of inactivity. Signing out removes it.
    </p>

    <h2>Location</h2>
    <p>
        The <em>Use my location</em> button asks the browser for a position, and only when pressed.
        The coordinates are sent to this server and forwarded to OpenWeatherMap to find the nearest
        station. They are not stored.
    </p>

    <h2>Weather lookups</h2>
    <p>
        City names you search are sent to OpenWeatherMap through this server. Searches are cached for a
        short period to reduce repeat calls; the cache is not tied to your account and is never used to
        build a profile.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>
        Use a disposable username and a unique password. If you want an account removed, ask the
        site operator to delete the row — there is no self-service deletion form yet.
    </p>
</div>
